cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "4i, explained interactively"
message: "If you use this explainer, please cite it as below, and cite the primary 4i papers listed in the references."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Lauryn Elise"
    family-names: "Bailey"
    affiliation: "Purvis Lab, Department of Genetics, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill"
    email: "lbailey@unc.edu"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/laelise/4i-explainer"
url: "https://laelise.github.io/4i-explainer/"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, single-file browser explainer for the chemistry of iterative
  indirect immunofluorescence imaging (4i): the covalent crosslinking that
  anchors antigens during fixation, the quenching chemistry that keeps antibody
  from being captured permanently, and the three-part elution buffer that
  removes antibody without removing the specimen.
keywords:
  - 4i
  - multiplexed imaging
  - immunofluorescence
  - science communication
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-08"
